# Question 3: Browser History — Linear Collection

**Problem Statement:**

A web browser stores recently visited pages. When the user presses the Back button, the most recently visited page should be removed first. Write a Java program using a linear collection to store browser history and implement the Back button using a Stack.

**Sample Input:**

```text
5
google.com
youtube.com
github.com
wikipedia.org
amazon.com
2
```

**Sample Output:**

```text
Browser History:
google.com
youtube.com
github.com
wikipedia.org
amazon.com

After pressing Back 2 times:
google.com
youtube.com
github.com
```

**Java Code:**

```java
import java.util.Scanner;
import java.util.Stack;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);

        Stack<String> history = new Stack<>();

        int n = sc.nextInt();
        sc.nextLine();

        // Store visited pages
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            String page = sc.nextLine();
            history.push(page);
        }

        System.out.println("Browser History:");
        for (String page : history) {
            System.out.println(page);
        }

        int back = sc.nextInt();

        // Press Back button
        for (int i = 0; i < back; i++) {
            if (!history.isEmpty()) {
                history.pop();
            }
        }

        System.out.println("\nAfter pressing Back "
                + back + " times:");

        for (String page : history) {
            System.out.println(page);
        }

        sc.close();
    }
}
```

**Concept Used:**

* **Stack:** Stores visited web pages.
* **Push:** Adds a newly visited page to the history.
* **Pop:** Removes the most recently visited page when Back is pressed.
* **LIFO (Last In, First Out):** The last page added is the first page removed.
